# [[ .ProjectName ]]

A production-ready Go REST API generated by [go-forge](https://github.com/akshadjaiswal/go-forge).

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Router | [chi](https://github.com/go-chi/chi) |
[[ if .WithAuth -]]
| Database | PostgreSQL + [sqlx](https://github.com/jmoiron/sqlx) |
| Auth | JWT ([golang-jwt/jwt](https://github.com/golang-jwt/jwt)) + bcrypt |
[[ end -]]
| Logging | Go 1.21+ `log/slog` (structured JSON) |
| Validation | [go-playground/validator](https://github.com/go-playground/validator) |
| Config | `.env` via [godotenv](https://github.com/joho/godotenv) |

## Setup

### 1. Prerequisites

- Go [[ .GoVersion ]]+
[[ if .WithAuth -]]
- PostgreSQL running locally (or via Docker)
[[ end ]]
### 2. Configure environment

```bash
cp .env.example .env
[[ if .WithAuth -]]
# Edit .env — set DATABASE_URL and JWT_SECRET
[[ end -]]
```

[[ if .WithAuth -]]
### 3. Create database

```bash
psql -U postgres -c "CREATE DATABASE [[ .DBName ]];"
```

### 4. Run migrations

```bash
make migrate
```

### 5. Start the server

```bash
make dev
```
[[ else -]]
### 3. Start the server

```bash
make dev
```
[[ end -]]

## Endpoints

| Method | Path | Auth | Description |
|--------|------|------|-------------|
| GET | `/health` | — | Health check |
[[ if .WithAuth -]]
| POST | `/auth/register` | — | Register a new user |
| POST | `/auth/login` | — | Login, returns JWT token |
| GET | `/users/{id}` | Bearer token | Get user by ID |
[[ end -]]

## Project structure

```
[[ .ProjectName ]]/
├── cmd/api/main.go          ← entry point
├── internal/
│   ├── config/              ← env var loading
│   ├── server/              ← chi router + route wiring
│   ├── handler/             ← HTTP handlers
[[ if .WithAuth -]]
│   ├── auth/                ← JWT service + middleware
│   ├── model/               ← domain structs
│   ├── repository/          ← sqlx DB queries
│   └── validator/           ← request validation helpers
[[ end -]]
├── pkg/
│   ├── logger/              ← slog setup
│   └── response/            ← JSON response helpers
[[ if .WithAuth -]]
├── migrations/              ← plain SQL migration files
[[ end -]]
├── api/requests.http        ← VS Code REST Client test file
└── Makefile                 ← dev, build, test, migrate targets
```

## Testing endpoints

Install the [REST Client](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=humao.rest-client) extension in VS Code, then open `api/requests.http` to send requests with a single click.
